NAME
       chvt - switch the active virtual console

SYNOPSIS
       chvt N

DESCRIPTION
       chvt makes console N the one shown on the screen and the one that
       receives the keyboard. Consoles 1-6 are text consoles (/dev/tty1 ..
       /dev/tty6), console 7 is the screen of a userspace display server
       while one holds it (SYS_DISPLAY_CLAIM).

       The same switch is available from the keyboard: Ctrl+Alt+F1 .. F6
       for the text consoles and Ctrl+Alt+F7 for the graphics. While a
       display server holds the screen, switching to text is refused. On a text
       console Alt+F1 .. F7 works without Ctrl.

       root may switch to any console. Other users may switch only from a
       process that runs on a text console.

EXAMPLES
       chvt 2
       chvt 7

SEE ALSO
       tty(1), getty(8), init(8)
